      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "title: \"Be careful what you vibe for\"\n",
        "author: \"Nicholas Dorsch\"\n",
        "date: today\n",
        "categories: [AI, opinion]\n",
        "image: media/the-dude.gif\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "I'm on the AI software development train like everyone else. I can't deny the\n",
        "productivity boost---it's too dramatic, too undeniable at this point to avoid---but a\n",
        "whole raft of new challenges is coming along for the ride, and I want to get some of my\n",
        "early thoughts down.\n",
        "\n",
        "I'm building a company, so I'm not just making weekend toys for personal use (although\n",
        "I've done some of that, [too](https://nick-dorsch.github.io/blog/posts/lex/)). My career\n",
        "and my reputation are on the line, I have skin in the game, so I can't just vibe and\n",
        "pray that the LLM slot machine keeps delivering what I need to provide value to clients,\n",
        "I need systems and guiding principles for navigating.\n",
        "\n",
        "This is doubly true for enterprise grade data systems, which is what I specialize in,\n",
        "but it applies to any project where your ass is on the line, and the reliable\n",
        "functioning of the system _actually matters_.\n",
        "\n",
        "I should state at the outset that I don't have decades of experience to draw from, my\n",
        "career is 9 years long, and programming has only been a part of that for about 5. I\n",
        "learn quickly, but I can't claim any special wisdom. \n",
        "\n",
        "I'm just trying to navigate responsibly. From what I've gathered, these challenges seem\n",
        "shared across a range of different experience levels.\n",
        "\n",
        "So, for whatever it's worth, I've been mentally noting my internal clench-o-meter for\n",
        "the last six months while doing different kinds of work, and I've started crystallizing\n",
        "some thoughts:\n",
        "\n",
        "## Software engineering and the Blues\n",
        "\n",
        "> _\"It's not the notes you play, it's the notes you don't play\"_\n",
        ">\n",
        "> --- Myles Davis (maybe)\n",
        "\n",
        "I've played guitar since I was 10.\n",
        "\n",
        "The thing about learning to play guitar, is that once you can play fast, you spend about\n",
        "10 years before you finally shut the fuck up.\n",
        "\n",
        "I shut the fuck up about 3 years ago, and nowadays I play blues, funk, and a bit of jazz\n",
        "and samba. Genre isn't the point, though.\n",
        "\n",
        "With the guitar, your fingers kind of... babble. Certain ergonomic shapes and patterns\n",
        "are the path of least resistance for your brain, so you end up repeating \"licks\" a lot.\n",
        "The problem is that those ergonomic patterns often don't map to sounds that people\n",
        "actually want to hear.\n",
        "\n",
        "Freebird is cool, Eddie Van Halen is cool, but sometimes... you know, just... shut the\n",
        "fuck up.\n",
        "\n",
        "I think we've all just been given the Devil's hands and become facemelting shredders,\n",
        "most of us without the decades of developing taste, and things are getting noisy. \n",
        "\n",
        "![People are going to _love_ hearing how fast I burn tokens with these new hands that\n",
        "literally everyone else also has now! (Art by Guiliano\n",
        "Bròcani)](media/devil-went-down-to-georgia.jpg)\n",
        "\n",
        "This will happen outside of software, too. It won't be long until the office is\n",
        "overflowing with the HTML equivalent of Freebird at max volume on repeat.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "```{=html}\n",
        "<div class=\"freebird-chaos\" aria-label=\"Maximum volume HTML chaos\">\n",
        "  <style>\n",
        "    .freebird-chaos {\n",
        "      position: relative;\n",
        "      margin: 2rem 0;\n",
        "      padding: 1.25rem;\n",
        "      border: 4px dashed #ff00aa;\n",
        "      background:\n",
        "        radial-gradient(circle at 20% 20%, #ffea00 0 10%, transparent 30%),\n",
        "        radial-gradient(circle at 80% 30%, #00f0ff 0 12%, transparent 32%),\n",
        "        linear-gradient(135deg, #130013, #2d001a 40%, #001b2d);\n",
        "      color: #fff;\n",
        "      font-family: \"Impact\", \"Arial Black\", system-ui, sans-serif;\n",
        "      text-transform: uppercase;\n",
        "      overflow: hidden;\n",
        "      box-shadow: 0 0 20px #ff00aa, 0 0 40px #ff5e00;\n",
        "      animation: ampShake 0.08s infinite alternate;\n",
        "    }\n",
        "\n",
        "    .freebird-chaos .title {\n",
        "      font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 5vw, 2.8rem);\n",
        "      letter-spacing: 0.12em;\n",
        "      text-shadow: 0 0 8px #fff, 0 0 24px #ff4d00, 0 0 42px #ff00aa;\n",
        "      animation: neonPulse 0.25s infinite alternate;\n",
        "    }\n",
        "\n",
        "    .freebird-chaos .riff {\n",
        "      margin-top: 0.65rem;\n",
        "      white-space: nowrap;\n",
        "      overflow: hidden;\n",
        "      font-size: clamp(1rem, 3.4vw, 1.6rem);\n",
        "      color: #ffea00;\n",
        "      text-shadow: 0 0 10px #ff7a00;\n",
        "      background: none;\n",
        "    }\n",
        "\n",
        "    .freebird-chaos .riff-track {\n",
        "      display: inline-flex;\n",
        "      width: max-content;\n",
        "      animation: soloRun 12s linear infinite;\n",
        "    }\n",
        "\n",
        "    .freebird-chaos .riff-track span {\n",
        "      padding-right: 2rem;\n",
        "    }\n",
        "\n",
        "    .freebird-chaos .fire {\n",
        "      margin-top: 0.8rem;\n",
        "      font-size: clamp(1.2rem, 4vw, 2rem);\n",
        "      filter: drop-shadow(0 0 8px #ff2a00);\n",
        "      animation: fireDance 0.25s infinite steps(2);\n",
        "    }\n",
        "\n",
        "    .freebird-chaos .strobe {\n",
        "      position: absolute;\n",
        "      inset: 0;\n",
        "      pointer-events: none;\n",
        "      background: repeating-linear-gradient(\n",
        "        -45deg,\n",
        "        transparent 0 18px,\n",
        "        rgba(255,255,255,0.11) 18px 22px\n",
        "      );\n",
        "      mix-blend-mode: screen;\n",
        "      animation: strobeSweep 0.6s linear infinite;\n",
        "    }\n",
        "\n",
        "    @keyframes ampShake {\n",
        "      from { transform: translate(0, 0) rotate(-0.2deg); }\n",
        "      to   { transform: translate(1px, -1px) rotate(0.2deg); }\n",
        "    }\n",
        "\n",
        "    @keyframes neonPulse {\n",
        "      from { transform: scale(1); }\n",
        "      to   { transform: scale(1.03); }\n",
        "    }\n",
        "\n",
        "    @keyframes soloRun {\n",
        "      from { transform: translateX(0); }\n",
        "      to   { transform: translateX(-50%); }\n",
        "    }\n",
        "\n",
        "    @keyframes fireDance {\n",
        "      from { transform: translateY(0) scale(1); }\n",
        "      to   { transform: translateY(-2px) scale(1.05); }\n",
        "    }\n",
        "\n",
        "    @keyframes strobeSweep {\n",
        "      from { transform: translateX(-30px); }\n",
        "      to   { transform: translateX(30px); }\n",
        "    }\n",
        "  </style>\n",
        "\n",
        "  <div class=\"strobe\"></div>\n",
        "  <div class=\"title\">🔥 Freebird.html @ MAX VOLUME EVERIDAY 4EVA YEEEEEEEEEAAAAAAAH 🔥</div>\n",
        "  <div class=\"riff\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n",
        "    <div class=\"riff-track\">\n",
        "      <span>DIDDLEDEDO-DIDDLEDEDO-DIDDLEDEDO • WEEEWEEWEEEWEEE • DIDDLEDEDO-DIDDLEDEDO • FACE-MELT MODE ENGAGED • DIDDLEDEDO-DIDDLEDEDO-DIDDLEDEDO • </span>\n",
        "      <span>DIDDLEDEDO-DIDDLEDEDO-DIDDLEDEDO • WEEEWEEWEEEWEEE • DIDDLEDEDO-DIDDLEDEDO • FACE-MELT MODE ENGAGED • DIDDLEDEDO-DIDDLEDEDO-DIDDLEDEDO • </span>\n",
        "      <span>DIDDLEDEDO-DIDDLEDEDO-DIDDLEDEDO • WEEEWEEWEEEWEEE • DIDDLEDEDO-DIDDLEDEDO • FACE-MELT MODE ENGAGED • DIDDLEDEDO-DIDDLEDEDO-DIDDLEDEDO • </span>\n",
        "    </div>\n",
        "  </div>\n",
        "  <div class=\"fire\">🔥🔥🔥🔥 🦅🎸🦅🎸🦅🎸🦅🎸🦅 🔥🔥🔥🔥</div>\n",
        "</div>\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "Can you feel the future yet?\n",
        "\n",
        "My point is... we probably all need to learn restraint. The best blues players know when\n",
        "to flex their chops, but can still transport you to another dimension with the right\n",
        "four note phrase.\n",
        "\n",
        "Good blues playing is all about leaving space, tension and release, restraint. Play\n",
        "less, feel more. It is considered. It's not automatic. It's not a stream of tokens.\n",
        "\n",
        "The actual _feel_ of the blues is subtle in execution and maybe not well understood by\n",
        "the casual listener. It's all about micro bends up to a critical zone between the minor\n",
        "and major third and seventh, all ascent, _never_ descent (that kills the effect),\n",
        "vibrato in the right places, dynamics, space... subtle things that combine to tingle our\n",
        "souls and makes us happy to be sad, or sad to be happy... but we share it, and it feels\n",
        "like things will be alright.\n",
        "\n",
        "It takes a long time to develop that subtlety, you can't really fake it. It takes\n",
        "_work_.\n",
        "\n",
        "AI is going to let us skip that work, if we don't want to do it... But I don't think\n",
        "that will go well, in art, in music, in science or in engineering.\n",
        "\n",
        "## The LLMs are following token streams, not your intentions\n",
        "\n",
        "> _\"They know the words but not the music.\"_\n",
        ">\n",
        "> ---Robert Hare, _Without Conscience_ (encountered in Peter Watts' _Blindsight_)\n",
        "\n",
        "For any feature I develop, I find myself thinking that I want to get to it with as\n",
        "little code as possible. The more services and unused code paths I let creep in, the\n",
        "faster the code expands beyond my cognition, and I'm back at _Freebird_ again.\n",
        "\n",
        "This has led me to favour database centric design for data workloads (avoiding\n",
        "application logic in favour of views and RPCs), which I know is controversial in the\n",
        "web-dev community, at least, but for my domain it leads to less code and keeps system\n",
        "understanding high. \n",
        "\n",
        "_No business logic in the database!_ is what I see... but sorry, my system works too\n",
        "well for me to listen.\n",
        "\n",
        "A SQL file, even if you don't like the syntax, is a very self-contained and well-behaved\n",
        "piece of logic. There is no ambiguity about the data contract coming in, the execution\n",
        "plan inside, and the data contract coming out, because it is all internal to its own\n",
        "system. The database just says _\"here you go\"_ or _\"no can do\"_, and it will work\n",
        "forever once you get it right, because the system's internal contracts are solid as a\n",
        "rock.[^plan-flip]\n",
        "\n",
        "This makes a web API a pass-through of what the database is doing. There are obviously\n",
        "cases where this can't work, like authentication flows, but if I can do it, it's my\n",
        "favoured approach.\n",
        "\n",
        "Compare that to an application based data workload... and suddenly you have external\n",
        "dependencies, error handling, and data being generated somewhere else on the network,\n",
        "which needs to get back to the database. That means distributed systems\n",
        "challenges---incomplete execution, invalid state, cache invalidation---I like to avoid\n",
        "all that (if I can), because it's just simpler, that way. \n",
        "\n",
        "I have the luxury of focussing on the C and A in\n",
        "[CAP](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CAP_theorem)[^ddia], because of the kind of problems I work\n",
        "on (lucky me).\n",
        "\n",
        "My point here is... The LLM isn't giving me this without extra, careful work. You could\n",
        "sneeze on your keyboard and come back 5 minutes later to a full backend API written in\n",
        "Python, and if you don't have strong opinions on the matter you might say \"LGTM\" and\n",
        "keep moving forward.\n",
        "\n",
        "I'm not kidding when I say that I have generated and deleted entire backend Web APIs\n",
        "from a few of my projects, multiple times, because I let the LLM vibe, but I just didn't\n",
        "like the way it was doing things.\n",
        "\n",
        "That experience is why, if I notice I'm just accepting everything the robot is giving\n",
        "me, my clench-o-meter spikes, and I [slow the fuck\n",
        "down](https://mariozechner.at/posts/2026-03-25-thoughts-on-slowing-the-fuck-down/).\n",
        "Because I don't have an opinion, which means I'm not ready to proceed. I'll come back\n",
        "when I have one.\n",
        "\n",
        "The model knows all the words, but it can't hear your music. So slow down, or get\n",
        "slopped.\n",
        "\n",
        "## What parts of your system are slop-tolerant?\n",
        "\n",
        "All vibes are not created equal. Different parts of your system are more or less\n",
        "resilient to the slop, and their tolerance depends on where they sit in the\n",
        "interconnected network of computation and logical dependency that couples data storage,\n",
        "transformation, interactivity and presentation in your system.\n",
        "\n",
        "You can shake a few branches up in the canopy, and sure, some HTML artifacts leaves\n",
        "might fall down... but who cares? Vibe your throwaway HTML docs, vibe your plots, you'd\n",
        "be crazy to hand write them at this point. The rest of the tree won't notice. Just go\n",
        "easy on the _Freebird_.\n",
        "\n",
        "Your frontend interface... buttons, widgets, styling... well, you can vibe it, but you\n",
        "might not love the results, so taking your time is still worthwhile. A badly coded hook\n",
        "might not perform well in client browsers, maybe React is rendering everything twice...\n",
        "maybe there's jitter in navigation... but that isn't all systems red, it's just not\n",
        "ideal. \n",
        "\n",
        "Taken to an extreme, an absolute nightmare of vibe coded spaghetti for a frontend is...\n",
        "bad, obviously, but its not armageddon, either. You can saw off your frontend completely\n",
        "and the trunk and roots of your system can remain. If you were in that situation, would\n",
        "you try and fix the nightmare, or just start again? I know what I'd do.\n",
        "\n",
        "So your frontend is, relatively at least, slop tolerant. Vibe away.\n",
        "\n",
        "What about your backend?\n",
        "\n",
        "Your API doesn't really care about your frontend, just send the response back and\n",
        "shut-up, or don't, don't care. If your frontend is slop, the backend has rate limiting\n",
        "and CORS to protect against the worst consequences of that.\n",
        "\n",
        "But now there is a lot more slop exposure. What if your backend is shit? Maybe several\n",
        "downstream services all depend on it. What if you want to completely rework the API\n",
        "design, six months later when you look closely at it, and cry? Now you're chainsawing\n",
        "the trunk of the tree, or grafting a new trunk to it, and it's not going to be fun. Your\n",
        "backend is not very slop tolerant. _Slow down and make carefully considered choices_, do\n",
        "not _Freebird_ that shit.\n",
        "\n",
        "... And your database?\n",
        "\n",
        "_... Laaawwwwwwwwwwwwd._\n",
        "\n",
        "If you vibe code your database, and your system is not so simple you could run it out of\n",
        "a google sheet, you better start mentally preparing yourself for the slop-pocalypse,\n",
        "because the database is your root system, and _vibes_ at that level of stability is\n",
        "otherwise known as a _fucking earthquake_, my guy.\n",
        "\n",
        "Zero slop tolerance. Zero. \n",
        "\n",
        "Every table. Every column. Every constraint. Every decision. If you are not on top of\n",
        "all of it, you are asking for serious trouble. If a composite unique constraint is left\n",
        "out or misspecified on an important table, for example, (a tiny, one line, easy to miss\n",
        "mistake), and you plow ahead with data ingestion, the rest of the system is all cooked. \n",
        "\n",
        "How many checks will downstream application logic need to run when they can't rely on\n",
        "the database's model of how the data works? Have fun watching your LLM committing 1000s\n",
        "of extra lines of code, working around your mistakes. \n",
        "\n",
        "You might say, _Nick, we just fix it up in the database, it's one migration script, it's\n",
        "not a big deal._\n",
        "\n",
        "We're living in the vibe-coding era, guys.\n",
        "\n",
        "1. LLM writes a new backend route for your API\n",
        "2. LLM writes a test verifying intended behaviour... the database data is wrong, so the\n",
        "   test fails\n",
        "3. LLM starts writing \n"
      ],
      "id": "f829457b"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "try DoSomething.PerfectlyReasonable.ThatShouldNeverFail:\n",
        "  if ('FUCKING_SLOP') in Database.EarlyHighCommitmentDecisions:\n",
        "    raise SlopException:\n",
        "      print(\"Why would you do this. Falling back to...\")\n"
      ],
      "id": "aedff276",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "...everywhere in your API code\n",
        "4. LLM learns the pattern and keeps doing this on repeat\n",
        "5. _Freebird_\n",
        "\n",
        "I'm sorry, does your LLM look through your database schema \n",
        "\n",
        "The most _insane_, _unhinged_ shit I have ever seen an LLM do while vibe coding is\n",
        "usually surrounding the database. I think because databases are so stateful, and LLM's\n",
        "understand the \n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "[^plan-flip]: Until a [query plan\n",
        "flip](https://clerk.com/blog/2026-02-19-system-outage-postmortem) brings your platform\n",
        "to a grinding half, at least. More reason for extreme care.\n",
        "[^ddia]: Yeah, I picked up that second edish of _Designing Data Intensive Applications_."
      ],
      "id": "e926f227"
    }
  ],
